      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, good point. I measured it and added the results to the commit\nmessage.\n\nEnd to end, serving a clone of linux.git (12M objects, 6.6 GB, with\nbitmap) from a JGit HTTP server, the counting phase got about 0.4 s\nslower (+4%), roughly 1% of the 41 s total. Total time and CPU stayed\nwithin run-to-run noise.\n\nI also ran a JMH benchmark of the addObject() bookkeeping alone. The\nextra hash bucket scan costs about 15% of that step, 0.4 s for 20M\nobjects, with no extra allocation.\n\nI didn\u0027t set up 1M refs: addObject() runs once per object in the pack,\nso the number of refs doesn\u0027t change this cost. Happy to run it if you\nstill want that data point.",
